{
  "rules": [
    "Persistent upward bias in errors: model forecasts are systematically too low versus realized prices, especially from ~day 15 onward. Apply a positive level shift that increases with horizon (small in week 1, larger in weeks 3–4).",
    "Trend/acceleration underreaction: when the recent history shows a turn from decline to rebound, the model lags the upswing by ~3–7 days. Add a momentum term based on the last 5–10 day slope/return to pull the path upward earlier.",
    "Late-horizon catch-up missing: true outcomes exhibit sustained rallies into days ~20–30, while the model stays range-bound/mean-reverting. Reduce mean-reversion strength beyond ~2 weeks; allow drift to persist when recent volatility + positive slope are present.",
    "Convexity error after breakouts: once prices break above the recent 30d range, realized prices continue trending higher; the model caps/plateaus. Add a breakout rule: if spot > 20–30d moving average and > prior 10d high, uplift weeks 3–4 forecasts by an additional premium.",
    "Horizon-specific correction heuristic: +0 to +0.5 EUR (days 1–7), +1 to +2 EUR (days 8–14), +3 to +5 EUR (days 15–30), scaled by recent 10d momentum (e.g., multiply by 1 + k*momentum)."
  ]
}
